<meta property="og:description" content="The Times of India took one of India’s most recognisable election symbols and moved it from the polling booth to the newspaper page. Ink of Democracy campaign, created with Havas Creative India for the 2024 Indian General Elections, used purple ink in print to speak to voters before they reached the polling station. The campaign"/>  
